==Strategy==
Treat this stage as a more aggressive version of [[Star Ocean]], as the premise is the exact same. You'll want to beat the stage before the extremely buffed Doge Darks and Gabriels enter the stage, since it would be near impossible to get rid of them once they're here.

Since this stage revolves around clearing the stage quickly, there is no point in stalling for cash. The waves of Doge Darks and Gabriels provide a lot anyways.

Units like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut]] or the newly obtained [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]] can and will work extremely well as backliners here, due to their high dps and area attack, able to wipe the peons before they become a major threat, while spammable units like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris]] or [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman]] can also work extremely well. (Do be mindful however that Cameraman must be in true form to work here.)

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Generally, any [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rusher]] [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]], or an Uber with a [[Special Abilities|special ability]] against [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]], [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]], or [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies should do well here. Some good examples are [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]], [[Snow Angel Twinstars (Uber Rare Cat)|Snow Angel Twinstars]] and [[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Empress Chronos]].

